1. Smoke may launch NOW, without waiting for the fold or for report 016. I checked: every r5 finding cites eval/kaggle/classify_rows.py or its tests. The only agent_timing.py reference is a citation of stock behaviour, not a defect. The classifier runs offline on raw timing.jsonl, so it has no effect on what the kernel executes. Preconditions: bundle 31b-v009 d38c55c7.. unchanged; ids from eval/plans/007-smoke-ids.txt; budget 5400 s; kernel code at a commit containing no rev5-fold changes; quota logged before and after (dec 064 item 4). If the fold diff turns out to touch agent_timing.py or any kernel/runner path, the smoke must use the pre-fold commit. Name that commit in the journal.
2. Seal the outputs. On download, record sha256 of timing.jsonl and every raw output file in ops/journal.md and ops/budget/kaggle.md BEFORE any analysis. Until the re-frozen classifier has a Director note, you may compute and look at ONLY: vLLM up (y/n), row count, rows parse (y/n), per-task wall/total seconds (for --seed-max and main budget sizing), and the COUNT of H-* rows under the current rev-4 classifier a208a023 (H count only, via a script that prints no PASS/FAIL/resolved values). Do not look at pass/fail/resolved values or patches.
