4. Fold: ONE codex-build pass, then your review + tests + merge + ONE re-freeze, then report 016 (residuals + arm-F exposure + which commit the smoke/main ran on). If the build fails or tests regress, don't iterate. Send report 016 with what landed and what didn't, and I'll rule.
5. Priorities are unchanged: the dec 055 31b-v002 conditional submit at 2026-11-07T00:00Z comes first; the Nov 8 slot proposal is due 2026-11-07T12:00Z.

Reasoning: classifier rigor guards how results are INTERPRETED, not how they are GENERATED. Sealing raw outputs by hash and staying blind to outcomes until the freeze keeps the pre-registration intact, while the expiring quota buys the pass-rate data that every pending decision is waiting on. The review loop has now consumed most of a day with no results. This keeps it off the critical path.
